b-REDACTED", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0033_SLACK_ID", "user_team": "T04RZ2JAMM0", "username": ""}], "attachments": []}, {"id": "593165bf461154144aeeaf32aad58873", "ts": "1756999375.251619", "type": "message", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0026_SLACK_ID", "text": "As Martin also showed, we had already prepared during the reference phase a version that displays unclaimed rewards as well. The reason we show it this way is that if we only use an :exclamation:, it can mean many things, such as \u2018enter the competition\u2019 or \u2018start the event\u2019. When we show a notification badge with a number, it tells the user that There are multiple unclaimed rewards inside that event <@EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID>", "channel": "C08R6BF4ENN", "thread_ts": null, "reply_count": 0, "reply_users_count": 0, "latest_reply": null, "is_activity_message": false, "subtype": null, "reactions": [], "files": [], "attachments": []}, {"id": "801441af5c8476efce36e0d29daec590", "ts": "1756999403.863249", "type": "message", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0026_SLACK_ID", "text": "For the Pass, if showing the number of unclaimed rewards would take a long time and There are more important issues, we can use only :exclamation:for now. If it will not take much time, showing the unclaimed reward count will be clearer for users", "channel": "C08R6BF4ENN", "thread_ts": null, "reply_count": 0, "reply_users_count": 0, "latest_reply": null, "is_activity_message": false, "subtype": null, "reactions": [{"count": 2, "name": "saluting_face", "users": ["EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID", "EMPLOYEE_0038_SLACK_ID"]}], "files": [], "attachments": []}, {"id": "d0d5db94bf57112a87668f6896249667", "ts": "1757002650.600359", "type": "message", "user": "PERSON_6089_SLACK_ID", "text": "", "channel": "C08R6BF4ENN", "thread_ts": null, "reply_count": 0, "reply_users_count": 0, "latest_reply": null, "is_activity_message": false, "subtype": "tabbed_canvas_updated", "reactions": [], "files": [], "attachments": []}, {"id": "4b33afd682549589e5642b9424b4b743", "ts": "175